36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It seems my concerns were well-founded. I found that support ownership was fragmented during the last outage, and our warehouse rules were rewritten twice mid-year. We really need a vendor who offers clear accountability and flexibility.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings are concerning. Our depots have no freeze window during peak season, and previous attempts at cutovers caused significant disruptions. Furthermore, our yard hardware is outdated and often bypassed by spreadsheets. We need a rugged, adaptable solution.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"My suspicions were spot on! We've been skipping upgrades since 2012 because we're too busy to test, and that 2018 data lift was a total mess that we spent a year cleaning up. We can't keep doing this.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"My findings are also worrying. We are losing half of our system experts to retirement this year, and hiring replacements is taking nearly a year. Our capacity to manage a transition is much lower than it appears.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we are all uncovering a rather charming tapestry of dysfunction. My findings suggest a preference for stealthy spending; while capital requests are trimmed, the recurring operating costs creep upward, particularly with those pesky add-on licenses.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"It really sounds like we are all seeing the same pattern of instability. @Benjamin, if costs are creeping up while support is fragmented, we might be paying more for less. We must prioritize a vendor with a single point of accountability.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, accountability is necessary, but it won't matter if the software can't run on our old hardware. We need a vendor that accepts our technical debt and the reality of our peak-season chaos.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, accepting technical debt is just a fancy way of saying we're settling for more patches. If we just ""adapt"" to the chaos, we'll be skipping upgrades for another decade. We need a clean break!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a clean break sounds ideal, but we lack the people to execute it. With our experts retiring and hiring stalled, a drastic change could collapse the current operations if the transition is too demanding.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, your point on human capacity is sobering. It seems we are caught between a desire for a clean slate and the reality of a skeleton crew, all while our operating budget quietly bleeds. A truly elegant solution would be one that minimizes both the transition's labor and the long-term financial surprises.","{""words"":52,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I agree with @Benjamin. We need a balance. Since we can't handle a chaotic transition or fragmented support, we should look for a vendor that provides strong managed services to fill our staffing gaps and a clear, single point of contact.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, managed services might help the office, but they won't fix the yard. If the vendor's tool requires modern handhelds we don't have, the floor will just go back to spreadsheets. Compatibility is non-negotiable.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, if we prioritize compatibility with junk hardware, we're just buying a fancy version of the same old problem. Why settle for a ""rugged"" failure when we could actually modernize? We need a vendor that forces us to grow up.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, forcing growth is risky when the people tasked with that growth are already stretched thin. If the system is too complex for the crews to adopt, they will simply ignore it, as they did in the last rollout.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, while I admire your enthusiasm for a digital awakening, forcing growth upon a starving crew is a recipe for disaster. We require a vendor whose pricing is as transparent as their implementation is gentle.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Midori,,"It seems we are all worried about different risks, but they all point to the same need: stability. We need a vendor that offers a gentle transition, clear accountability, and a realistic approach to our current constraints.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,Stability is only possible if the system survives the depot floor. I will support any candidate that proves they can integrate with our existing hardware and respect the peak-season calendar without causing a collapse.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm still leaning toward a clean break. If we just play it safe, we're just paying for a more expensive version of our own dysfunction. Let's see which candidates actually have the guts to fix this.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I hope we can find a candidate that doesn't underestimate the burden on our staff. A system that looks great on paper but fails in practice will only exhaust the few people we have left.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we have reached a consensus on our collective anxiety. I shall be looking for a candidate who offers a predictable cost structure, lest we find ourselves paying for a ""modernization"" that never actually ends.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
