60,3,,status,Misaki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the options, Meridian Systems seems the most balanced. Their fixed configuration and regional service team could provide the accountability and stability we need without overwhelming our remaining staff.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, Meridian's fixed configuration might be too rigid for our yard's reality. Anchor Industrial Software is more promising; they are built for transport and have engineers on-site, which is critical for surviving our peak-season cutover.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, Anchor is just more of the same! On-site engineers and our own servers? That's exactly how we ended up with a system from 2012 that we're too scared to upgrade. I'm looking at Tessera.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"@May, Tessera's reliance on a partner firm for training and migration worries me. With our experts retiring, we cannot risk a third party that doesn't understand our internal pressures. Anchor's on-site presence is more reassuring.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@May, while Tessera's marketplace sounds modern, it is a siren song for the very ""add-on"" cost creep I discovered. Corvus is a financial nightmare of separate licenses. I find Meridian's fixed configuration quite appealing for budget predictability.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, I understand the need for flexibility, but Anchor's on-premise model might just prolong our technical debt. Meridian's hosted suite offers a cleaner break while the regional team ensures we aren't left alone when things break.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, a hosted suite is useless if the yard scanners can't talk to it. Anchor's engineering team being present during rollout is the only way to ensure the system actually works on the floor before they leave.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you're obsessed with the floor, but you're ignoring the ceiling! Anchor is just a fancy way to stay stuck in the past. Tessera's cloud approach is the only way to stop the cycle of aging in place.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, a cloud approach is only a solution if the people can actually use it. If the training is outsourced to a partner, we risk another rollout where the crews simply ignore the new rules.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Misaki, your caution is well-placed. @May, your desire for progress is noble, but Tessera's marketplace is a playground for hidden fees. Meridian offers a hosted model that modernizes us without the financial volatility of a modular or marketplace approach.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, I agree. Meridian seems to be the safest middle ground. It addresses the accountability issue with a dedicated service team and avoids the chaos of a modular system or the risks of a partner-led migration.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Midori, safety is an illusion if the system fails during the November rush. Anchor's specialized focus on transport and their on-site engineering presence is the only realistic way to handle our hardware and calendar.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, you're just asking for a more expensive version of our current disaster! Anchor is a trap. Tessera is the only one that actually moves us forward. I'm not voting for a system that lives on our own racks.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@May, moving forward is pointless if the people are left behind. Anchor's on-site engineers provide the direct support our exhausted staff needs to actually adopt the system, rather than ignoring it.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, @Misaki, your preference for Anchor is understandable, yet on-premise systems often hide maintenance costs that bloom over time. Meridian provides the modernization May craves with the predictability I require. It is the most rational compromise.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Misaki"",""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I've listened to everyone, and while Anchor offers great on-site support, Meridian's hosted model provides the accountability and stability we need without the risks of on-premise debt. It's the most harmonious choice for our current situation. I vote Meridian.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I cannot ignore the risk of a total floor collapse during peak season. Only Anchor's transport specialization and on-site engineering presence provide the necessary safeguards for our hardware and calendar. I vote Anchor.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I'm not going to be part of a vote that keeps us trapped in the dark ages. We need a real change, not a polished version of our old mistakes. I vote Tessera.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I cannot support a transition that relies on outsourced training or rigid configurations while our internal expertise is vanishing. Anchor's on-site engineers are the only ones who can truly support our exhausted staff. I vote Anchor.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"While I appreciate the on-site comfort Anchor provides, I cannot ignore the long-term financial risk of on-premise maintenance and the volatility of Tessera's marketplace. Meridian is the only logical choice for budget stability. I vote Meridian.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
